Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.00,0:00:14.66,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I'd been driving for\Nalmost 11 hours when the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.66,0:00:16.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}detour signs pushed me off the interstate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.22,0:00:20.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The road narrowed to two\Nlanes, then the radio
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.00,0:00:22.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}lost its station, and for a long time the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.34,0:00:24.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}only light out there\Nwas my own headlights.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.22,0:00:28.86,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Around two in the morning, I saw a gas\Nstation sign glowing over the fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.54,0:00:34.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The pumps were on, the store was dark, and\Nthere was one other car parked by the air
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.06,0:00:36.86,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}machine with its engine\Nrunning and nobody inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.74,0:00:40.16,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}This was in October, about six years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.84,0:00:45.02,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I was 24 and moving back home to Missouri\Nafter a job in Colorado fell apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.00,0:00:49.38,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Everything I owned was in the backseat\Nof a Corolla with a cracked windshield.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.98,0:00:52.22,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I'd planned to stop for the\Nnight in a motel somewhere
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.22,0:00:54.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}in western Kansas, but I kept telling
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.80,0:00:57.82,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}myself one more hour, and\Nby the time the detour
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.82,0:00:59.72,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}came up, I was too tired to be smart
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.70,0:01:00.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.94,0:01:03.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I pulled up to the pump,\Nfarthest from the other car.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.00,0:01:07.94,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was an older station wagon, dark green\Nwith wood panels on the sides and a bumper
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.94,0:01:10.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}sticker that said, Proud\NParent of an Honor Student,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.24,0:01:11.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}with the name of the school scratched
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.50,0:01:12.30,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}off.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.42,0:01:14.30,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The exhaust was rising in the cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.76,0:01:16.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The headlights were off,\Nbut the dome light was
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.70,0:01:18.80,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}on, and I could see a\Njacket on the passenger
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.80,0:01:20.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}seat and a fast food bag on the dashboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.78,0:01:23.78,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I figured whoever it\Nbelonged to was in the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.78,0:01:24.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}bathroom around the side of the building.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.58,0:01:27.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I filled the tank and waited.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.20,0:01:28.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I don't know why I waited.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.76,0:01:32.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I think I wanted to see someone walk back\Nto that car, just so I could stop thinking
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.68,0:01:33.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.14,0:01:34.94,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Nobody came.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.40,0:01:37.44,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The pump clicked off,\Nthe screen asked if I
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.44,0:01:39.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}wanted a receipt, and the whole time that
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.76,0:01:43.36,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}engine kept idling, steady, like\Nit had been running for hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.12,0:01:45.72,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't go check the bathroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.08,0:01:47.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I got back in my car and left.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.60,0:01:52.42,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}About twenty minutes later, the\Ndetour signs ended at a truck stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.72,0:01:55.64,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was the first real building\NI'd seen in a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.24,0:01:58.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}A diner on one side, a\Ncouple of semis parked
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.76,0:02:00.94,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}out back with their running lights on, and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.94,0:02:04.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}a sign that said, Open 24 hours,\Nwith two of the letters burned out.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.76,0:02:07.66,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I parked near the\Nentrance because I needed
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.66,0:02:09.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}coffee, and I needed to sit somewhere with
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.88,0:02:10.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}people for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.18,0:02:15.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Inside, it was warm and smelled\Nlike burnt coffee and bacon grease.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.16,0:02:18.02,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}There was a trucker at\Nthe counter, reading
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.02,0:02:20.46,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}his phone, an older man asleep in a booth
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.46,0:02:21.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}by the window, and one waitress.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.80,0:02:25.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Her name tag said D.\NShe looked about fifty,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.82,0:02:27.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and she called me Honey\Nbefore I'd even sat
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.74,0:02:28.54,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}down.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.90,0:02:31.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I took a booth facing\Nthe door, ordered coffee
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.68,0:02:33.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and a slice of pie, and started looking at
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.70,0:02:38.04,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the map on my phone, trying to figure\Nout how far I was from anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.76,0:02:41.46,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}That's when the couple came in.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.96,0:02:44.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They were young, maybe my age.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.78,0:02:46.96,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The guy wore a gray\Nhoodie, and the girl had
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.96,0:02:49.12,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}on a denim jacket that\Nwas too thin for the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.12,0:02:49.92,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.76,0:02:52.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It had started to rain\Noutside, and the shoulders
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.14,0:02:53.56,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}of their jackets were dark with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.32,0:02:57.52,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They were arguing in that low,\Ntight way people argue in public.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.38,0:03:00.20,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}As they walked past my\Nbooth, the girl said,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.48,0:03:01.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Every single time, Ray.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.86,0:03:02.96,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Every single time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.76,0:03:04.56,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He didn't answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.24,0:03:07.58,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They sat two booths down\Nfrom me, across the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.58,0:03:09.98,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}aisle, and D. went over with menus and two
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.98,0:03:11.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}waters like it was nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.96,0:03:13.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't think much about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.16,0:03:14.96,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I ate my pie.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.54,0:03:17.90,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I heard bits of their\Nconversation, something about
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.90,0:03:20.26,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}a wrong turn and whose idea it had been
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.26,0:03:21.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}to leave so late.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.62,0:03:24.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The girl had a laugh that\Nwasn't really a laugh.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.84,0:03:26.90,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}At one point, Ray said, We'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.30,0:03:28.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}We're almost there.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.72,0:03:29.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She didn't say anything back.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.62,0:03:32.64,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}After a while, I got up\Nto use the restroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.94,0:03:35.22,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was at the end of a short\Nhallway past the kitchen.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.80,0:03:37.52,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I remember the hallway\Nbecause one of the fluorescent
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.52,0:03:39.02,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}lights was flickering, and there
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.02,0:03:42.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}was a corkboard on the wall with business\Ncards and a flyer for a missing dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.86,0:03:45.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I was in there maybe\Nthree or four minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.68,0:03:47.90,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I washed my hands,\Nsplashed water on my face,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.90,0:03:50.08,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and looked at myself in\Nthe mirror, thinking
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.08,0:03:51.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I really needed to find a bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.86,0:03:56.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}When I came out and walked back toward my\Nbooth, the bell over the front door rang.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.00,0:04:01.58,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was them, the same\Ncouple, gray hoodie, thin
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.58,0:04:03.94,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}denim jacket, the\Nshoulders of both jackets
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.94,0:04:04.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}dark with rain.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.38,0:04:07.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They walked in the same\Nway, him a step ahead,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.08,0:04:09.72,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}her a little behind with her arms crossed,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.90,0:04:15.52,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and as they passed me, the girl said,\NEvery single time, Ray, every single time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.28,0:04:17.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I stopped in the aisle.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.30,0:04:20.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I looked over at the booth two down\Nfrom mine, where they'd been sitting.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.16,0:04:22.04,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.86,0:04:25.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}No menus, no glasses, no\Nwet rings on the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.20,0:04:28.66,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It had been wiped down like\Nnobody had used it all night.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.38,0:04:31.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They sat in that same booth.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.94,0:04:34.44,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Dee came over with two\Nmenus and two waters, and
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.44,0:04:36.90,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}she smiled at them, and she said, Evening
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.90,0:04:37.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}you two.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.78,0:04:38.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Rough night out there?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.12,0:04:41.30,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Exactly how you'd greet\Nsomeone who just walked in.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.10,0:04:45.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I sat down because I didn't\Nknow what else to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.78,0:04:46.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}My coffee was still there.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.80,0:04:47.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}My plate was still there.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.28,0:04:49.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I watched them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.82,0:04:52.02,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I kept waiting for one\Nof them to look at me,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.08,0:04:54.26,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}or laugh, or for this to turn into some
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.26,0:04:55.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}kind of joke.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.98,0:04:56.98,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Ray was rubbing his eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.54,0:04:59.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The girl was looking out the\Nwindow at the parking lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.20,0:05:02.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They were having the same conversation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.26,0:05:04.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Wrong turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.38,0:05:05.18,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Leaving too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.24,0:05:07.08,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}And then Ray said, We'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.30,0:05:08.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}We're almost there.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.60,0:05:10.32,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I looked at the trucker at the counter.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.82,0:05:12.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He hadn't looked up from\Nhis phone the whole time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.74,0:05:15.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The old man in the window\Nbooth was still asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.52,0:05:19.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Nobody else in that room seemed\Nto think anything was wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.88,0:05:22.20,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I left a twenty on the\Ntable and walked out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.58,0:05:23.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't wait for change.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.82,0:05:27.30,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}When I got outside, the rain had\Nstopped, and the parking lot was dry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.70,0:05:28.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Completely dry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.08,0:05:29.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}No puddles.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.08,0:05:31.12,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Nothing wet on my windshield.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.48,0:05:34.44,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I stood there for a second,\Nlooking at the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.92,0:05:37.24,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Then I got in my car,\Nlocked the doors, and sat
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.24,0:05:39.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}with the engine running for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.68,0:05:43.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't want to drive past\Nthat gas station again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.72,0:05:45.28,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't want to go back inside, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.46,0:05:48.26,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}So I just sat there\Nuntil the sky started to
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.26,0:05:50.26,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}turn gray, and then I followed the signs
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.26,0:05:51.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}back to the interstate.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.76,0:05:54.40,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't pass the gas\Nstation on the way back.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.94,0:05:56.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I took the same road.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.18,0:05:56.98,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I'm sure of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.58,0:05:58.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It just wasn't there.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.38,0:06:02.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I had a dash cam back then,\None of those cheap ones
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.34,0:06:04.16,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}that records over itself every few hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.06,0:06:07.56,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}When I finally got home\Nand checked it, most
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.56,0:06:08.86,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}of that night had\Nalready been overwritten.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.68,0:06:12.44,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The only file left starts\Nas I pull into the truck
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.44,0:06:14.42,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}stop parking lot at 2.14 in the morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.32,0:06:18.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I park, the camera keeps\Nrecording, and about
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.00,0:06:20.22,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}a minute later, the dark\Ngreen station wagon
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.22,0:06:22.16,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}pulls into the spot right in front of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.36,0:06:25.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Engine running, dome\Nlight on, nobody inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.52,0:06:29.22,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The date on that clip is October 14th.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.58,0:06:32.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The year is the one before\NI ever drove that road.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.78,0:06:35.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I still drive that interstate\Na couple of times a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.38,0:06:38.66,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}If the detour signs are\Nup, I don't take them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.28,0:06:41.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I find the last town\Nbefore the exit, I park
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.70,0:06:43.96,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}somewhere well lit, and I sleep in my car
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.96,0:06:44.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}until morning.
